  "transformer": "The neural network architecture behind modern LLMs, built around attention.",
  "self-attention": "The mechanism that lets every token look at every other token in the input and decide which ones matter to it.",
  "multi-head attention": "Running several attention calculations in parallel, so each 'head' can focus on a different kind of relationship.",
  "positional encoding|RoPE": "Extra information added to tokens so the model knows their order in the sequence.",
  "encoder": "The part of a model that reads input and turns it into a representation. BERT is encoder-only.",
  "decoder": "The part of a model that generates text one token at a time. GPT-style LLMs are decoder-only.",

