  "embedding": "A list of numbers that captures the meaning of a piece of text, so similar meanings end up close together.",
  "embedding model": "A model that turns text into embeddings. Queries and documents must use the same one.",
  "vector database|vector store": "A database built to store embeddings and quickly find the ones closest to a query.",
  "cosine similarity": "A measure of how similar two embeddings are, based on the angle between them. 1 means same direction.",
  "semantic search": "Search by meaning using embeddings, so 'time off' can find 'leave policy' without shared words.",
  "BM25": "The classic keyword search ranking formula. Strong for exact terms like product codes and error IDs.",
  "hybrid search": "Running keyword (BM25) and vector search together and merging the results, to get both exact matches and meaning.",
  "reciprocal rank fusion|RRF": "A simple way to merge two ranked lists by position rather than by score, used in hybrid search.",
  "HNSW": "A popular index for fast approximate nearest-neighbour search. It builds a layered graph of vectors.",
  "IVF": "An index that groups vectors into clusters and only searches the nearest clusters, trading some recall for speed.",
  "approximate nearest neighbour|ANN": "Finding vectors that are very close to the query quickly, accepting that the exact closest might occasionally be missed.",
  "metadata filter": "Restricting a search by fields such as department, date, language or user permissions.",
  "chunk": "A small piece of a document, a few hundred tokens long, that is embedded and retrieved on its own. Splitting documents into chunks is RAG stage 2.",
  "chunking": "Splitting documents into chunks for retrieval. How you split decides what can be found.",
  "chunk overlap": "Repeating a little text between neighbouring chunks so a fact on a boundary isn't cut in half.",
