  "groundedness": "How well an answer is backed by its source documents. Much the same idea as faithfulness.",
  "answer relevance": "Whether the answer actually addresses the question that was asked.",
  "context precision": "A RAG metric: how much of what was retrieved is actually useful, and whether the useful parts are ranked near the top.",
  "context recall": "A RAG metric: whether retrieval brought back everything the answer needs.",
  "recall@k": "How often the correct chunk appears anywhere in the top k results.",
  "precision@k": "What fraction of the top k results are relevant.",
  "MRR": "Mean reciprocal rank: rewards the first correct result for being near the top (rank 1 scores 1, rank 2 scores 0.5, and so on).",
  "nDCG": "A ranking metric that rewards relevant results for appearing higher, with graded relevance.",
  "RAGAS": "An open-source library of RAG evaluation metrics such as faithfulness and context recall, mostly scored by an LLM judge.",
