  "RAG-Fusion": "Generate several versions of the question, search with each, and merge the result lists with RRF.",
  "multi-query|multi-query retrieval": { tip: "Searching with several rephrasings of the user's question to catch documents one wording would miss.", only: ["riq", "story"] },
  "RAPTOR": "A RAG method that clusters chunks and summarises them into a tree, so questions can be answered at detail level or summary level.",
  "LightRAG": "A lighter, cheaper form of GraphRAG that combines a knowledge graph with normal vector search.",
  "Speculative RAG": "A small, fast model drafts several answers from different retrieved subsets, and a larger model picks and checks the best one.",
  "LongRAG": "A RAG design that retrieves much larger units (whole sections or documents) because long-context models can read them.",
  "CAG|cache-augmented generation": "Instead of retrieving per question, load a small, fixed knowledge set into the prompt once and reuse it through the model's cache.",
