  "modular RAG": "RAG built from swappable parts (router, retrievers, rerankers, checkers) that can be arranged into different flows.",
  /* Security */
  "RBAC|role-based access control": "Giving permissions by role or group (for example 'Plant A engineers') rather than person by person.",
  "redaction|redact|redacted": "Removing or masking sensitive details (names, numbers, secrets) before text is stored or sent anywhere.",
  "Presidio": "Microsoft's open-source tool for finding and masking personal data (names, phone numbers, IDs) in text.",
  "Key Vault|secret manager": "A secure cloud service for storing passwords, API keys and certificates, instead of keeping them in code.",
  /* Backend, async and serving */
  "ASGI": "Asynchronous Server Gateway Interface: the Python web standard that lets one server handle many waiting requests at once. FastAPI uses it.",
  "WSGI": "Web Server Gateway Interface: the older Python web standard (used by Flask) where each worker handles one request at a time.",
  "event loop": "The scheduler at the heart of async Python: it runs one task until it has to wait, then switches to another that is ready.",
  "coroutine|coroutines": "A function defined with async def that can pause at await and let other work run meanwhile.",
  "SSE|server-sent events": "A simple way for a server to push a stream of messages over one open HTTP connection, used to stream tokens to a chat UI.",
  "Uvicorn": "A fast ASGI server that runs FastAPI apps.",
