  "FAISS": "Meta's open-source library for fast vector search inside your own program. Very fast, but not a database: no server or permissions.",
  "Pinecone": "A fully managed, cloud-hosted vector database service. No servers to run; data lives in the vendor's cloud.",
  "Chroma|ChromaDB": "A lightweight open-source vector database that runs in a few lines of Python. Popular for prototypes and small apps.",
  "Weaviate": "An open-source vector database with built-in hybrid search and modules for embedding models. Self-hosted or managed cloud.",
  "Milvus": "An open-source vector database designed for very large scale, up to billions of vectors, across many machines.",
  "Qdrant": "An open-source vector database written in Rust, known for efficient filtered vector search. Self-hosted or managed cloud.",
  "OpenSearch": "An open-source fork of Elasticsearch, led by AWS. Similar keyword and vector search features.",
